{"translation":{"id":"deu_l12","name":"Lutherbibel 1912","website":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=deu1912","licenseUrl":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=deu1912","licenseNotes":null,"shortName":"L12","englishName":"German Luther Bible 1912","language":"deu","textDirection":"ltr","sha256":"c37943923929f9d47f5299e633d5ee935792894e7e3db2bcce52e717d645458e","availableFormats":["json"],"listOfBooksApiLink":"/api/deu_l12/books.json","numberOfBooks":66,"totalNumberOfChapters":1189,"totalNumberOfVerses":31102,"languageName":"Deutsch","languageEnglishName":"German"},"book":{"id":"PSA","translationId":"deu_l12","name":"Psalmen","commonName":"Psalmen","title":"Die Psalmen","order":19,"numberOfChapters":150,"sha256":"fec3ad12d0d95047286c01c2d39f8eb0a40702c64def30b525e8759548401bce","firstChapterNumber":1,"firstChapterApiLink":"/api/deu_l12/PSA/1.json","lastChapterNumber":150,"lastChapterApiLink":"/api/deu_l12/PSA/150.json","totalNumberOfVerses":2461},"chapter":{"number":137,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":[{"text":"An den Wassern zu Babel saßen wir und weinten, wenn wir an Zion gedachten.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Unsere Harfen hingen wir an die Weiden, die daselbst sind.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Denn dort hießen uns singen, die uns gefangen hielten, und in unserm Heulen fröhlich sein: “Singet uns ein Lied von Zion!”","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Wie sollten wir des HERRN Lied singen in fremden Landen?","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Vergesse ich dein, Jerusalem, so werde ich meiner Rechten vergessen.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Meine Zunge soll an meinem Gaumen kleben, wo ich nicht dein gedenke, wo ich nicht lasse Jerusalem meine höchste Freude sein.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"HERR, gedenke der Kinder Edom den Tag Jerusalems, die da sagten: “Rein ab, rein ab bis auf ihren Boden!”","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Du verstörte Tochter Babel, wohl dem, der dir vergilt, wie du uns getan hast!","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Wohl dem, der deine jungen Kinder nimmt und zerschmettert sie an dem Stein!","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/deu_l12/PSA/137.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/deu_l12/PSA/138.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/deu_l12/PSA/136.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":9}